==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|catatony||dated}}

===Etymology===
From {{w|international scientific vocabulary}}, from German {{m|de|Katatonie}}, from {{bor|en|NL.|catatonia}}, from a Greek word meaning to stretch tight; {{l|en|surface analysis#Noun}}, {{confix|en|cata|tonus|alt2=tone|ia}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/kætəˈtoʊniə/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# A severe [[psychiatric]] condition, often associated with [[schizophrenia]], characterized by a [[tendency]] to remain in a [[rigid]] state of [[stupor]] for long [[period]]s which give way to short periods of extreme [[agitation]].
# {{lb|en|informal}} A frozen, unresponsive state, as of electronic equipment.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1998|author=David Drake|author2=Thomas T. Thomas|title=Crisis of Empire Book I: An Honorable Defense
|passage=“Relay that!” Thwaite shouted. Somewhere on the bridge a hand closed over a relay and dropped the AIDs into an electronic '''catatonia'''.}}

